From: Ethan Hill <ethan.hill1999@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:52:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] KitKat UI P37: shadow gradient navbar scrim on
 homescreen and solid black navbar in apps

Re-land of the 2026-11-04 'Nav bar shadow attempt' (the hand-forged
patches/frameworks-base/0019) as a real commit: the stored patch had
placeholder hunk headers and could never apply - candyos-verify
died on it. Implemented against the tree as it actually is:

- DisplayPolicy.adjustWindowParamsLw forces
  FLAG_TRANSLUCENT_NAVIGATION on home-activity windows, so the
  launcher draws behind the bar and the navbar enters translucent
  mode on the homescreen: NavigationBarTransitions then renders the
  P35 nav_bar_kitkat_scrim.xml gradient over the wallpaper instead
  of the opaque bar. The attempt's win.isHomeWindow() does not
  exist in this tree; the activity type is the real check, and
  adjustWindowParamsLw runs from addWindow before the flags are
  first consulted.

- The attempt's second half (BarBackground mOpaque pinned to solid
  black) is already the tree state: SystemUI
  system_bar_background_opaque is #ff000000, so that hunk is a
  no-op and is not carried.

Change-Id: I6b4ac25c0fa49c7b2a6d9d43711198bd011aeedb
---
 .../core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayPolicy.java    | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayPolicy.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayPolicy.java
index 91fc05043155..9bd22c683680 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayPolicy.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayPolicy.java
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 
 package com.android.server.wm;
 
+import static android.app.WindowConfiguration.ACTIVITY_TYPE_HOME;
 import static android.app.WindowConfiguration.WINDOWING_MODE_FREEFORM;
 import static android.inputmethodservice.InputMethodService.ENABLE_HIDE_IME_CAPTION_BAR;
 import static android.view.Display.TYPE_INTERNAL;
@@ -970,6 +971,13 @@ public class DisplayPolicy {
      * are modified in-place.
      */
     public void adjustWindowParamsLw(WindowState win, WindowManager.LayoutParams attrs) {
+        // KitKat UI Project (P37): force translucent navigation on the home
+        // window so the launcher draws behind the nav bar and the bar renders
+        // the 4.4 shadow gradient scrim (nav_bar_kitkat_scrim.xml) over the
+        // wallpaper instead of an opaque bar.
+        if (win.getActivityType() == ACTIVITY_TYPE_HOME) {
+            attrs.flags |= WindowManager.LayoutParams.FLAG_TRANSLUCENT_NAVIGATION;
+        }
         switch (attrs.type) {
             case TYPE_SYSTEM_OVERLAY:
             case TYPE_SECURE_SYSTEM_OVERLAY:
